<%- include('../partials/header', { title: 'Installs & usage' }) %>
<div class="admin-bar">
  <h1>Installs &amp; usage</h1>
  <a href="/admin">&larr; Dashboard</a>
</div>
<p class="muted">An anonymous count: each phone keeps a random code in its own storage and reports once a day whether it opened the site as the installed app or in a browser. No names, accounts or addresses are stored. Counting began <%= stats.firstSeen ? stats.firstSeen.slice(0, 10) : 'with the first visit after this was added' %>.</p>

<div class="table-scroll">
<table class="admin-table usage-totals">
  <tbody>
    <tr><th>Phones with the app installed</th><td><strong><%= stats.installedDevices %></strong></td><td class="muted">Installed (reported by the browser) or opened from the home-screen icon</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Opened the app today</th><td><strong><%= stats.appToday %></strong></td><td class="muted">Phones, New Zealand day</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Opened the app in the last 7 days</th><td><strong><%= stats.appWeek %></strong></td><td class="muted"></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Browser-only phones</th><td><strong><%= stats.webOnlyDevices %></strong></td><td class="muted">Use the website but never opened the installed app</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Install confirmations</th><td><strong><%= stats.installEvents %></strong></td><td class="muted">Android Chrome, Edge and Samsung send these; iPhone and Firefox don't</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p class="muted">An iPhone keeps separate storage for the home-screen app, so it can appear once under browser-only and once under installed. Clearing a phone's browser data also makes it count as a new phone.</p>

<h2>Last 14 days</h2>
<div class="table-scroll">
<table class="admin-table">
  <thead><tr><th>Day</th><th>App phones</th><th>Browser phones</th><th>New app phones</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <% stats.days.forEach(d => { %>
      <tr><td><%= d.day %></td><td><%= d.app %></td><td><%= d.web %></td><td><%= d.newApp %></td></tr>
    <% }) %>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<% if (stats.breakdown.length) { %>
  <h2>Installed phones by browser</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll">
  <table class="admin-table">
    <thead><tr><th>Phone</th><th>Browser</th><th>Count</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <% stats.breakdown.forEach(b => { %>
        <tr><td><%= b.platform %></td><td><%= b.browser %></td><td><%= b.n %></td></tr>
      <% }) %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
<% } %>

<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
